# Cache-Control for the static site, applied by the asset router.
#
# Only one rule, deliberately. Overlapping rules in this file are additive:
# a request matching two rules gets both values joined with a comma, so a
# `/*` rule here would turn the line below into "immutable, no-cache" and
# mean neither.
#
# The HTML needs nothing. Cloudflare already serves assets with
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which is exactly right for the app
# shell: revalidate before every use, so a deploy is visible immediately.
#
# These rules do NOT apply to responses from the Worker itself. Anything in
# wrangler's `run_worker_first` list (serving endpoints, the tool API, /mcp,
# /docs) is generated by our code and sets its own headers.

# Vite fingerprints these filenames by content, so a changed file is a
# changed URL and this can never go stale. Without it, the default makes a
# browser revalidate every script and stylesheet on every page load for no
# benefit whatsoever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
